  "observations": "All five conjugate-then-affine warm and cloned pairs are slower, and those sample ranges do not overlap the baseline ranges. Other ranges sometimes overlap; no statistical significance claim is made. Affine and pi-transport queries allocate more, while some opaque construction controls allocate less. Retained-byte and peak-byte medians are unchanged across the full matrix.",
  "inspection_hypothesis": "The trial materializes a zero coefficient even for a rational-only intermediate, then may discard it when an ordinary rational square-root leaf lacks a retained certificate. Investigate representing the radical as optional and using the same exact square reduction as the existing recognizer for rational square-root leaves. This is a source-inspection hypothesis, not a measured attribution.",
  "next_step": "Fork the rejected source, preserve all guards and probes, and evaluate a narrower temporary representation plus exact rational-root handling. Repeat complete scalar qualification and the same fixed cost matrix before considering consumer gates.",
